            "bodyHtml": "<p>Complete the notes below. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p><div><div>The Patagon People of South America</div><p>Clothing</p><ul><li>one type of coat is culturally important</li><li>young guanaco were used to make the coats because of their {{31}} skin</li><li>men hunted the guanaco</li><li>women sewed the skins together into coats</li><li>scrapers made from {{32}} are today displayed in museums</li><li>colours from natural {{33}} were used</li></ul><p>The Arrival of the Spanish</p><ul><li>more guanaco were caught because of the use of the {{34}} for hunting</li><li>coats played a {{35}} role rather than just being for personal use</li><li>new materials such as {{36}} improved the scraping process</li></ul><p>Conclusions</p><ul><li>coat designs date from pre-historic times — similar designs are found inside {{37}}</li><li>coat designs may have been a link with people's {{38}}</li><li>large Patagon settlements were not built on the {{39}}</li><li>shepherds still make {{40}} using similar techniques</li></ul></div>",
